---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/PageHead.astro';
import { profile } from '../data/profile';
---

<Layout title="Sources & verification">
  <PageHead
    eyebrow="Editorial transparency"
    title="Grounded in public sources."
    intro="A record of the materials used for this unofficial design concept, reviewed October 28, 2026."
  />
  <div class="wrap narrow sources-content section-bottom">
    <h2>Primary materials</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>
        <a href={profile.original}>Personal website · Home</a>: name,
        appointment, professional email, interests, and homepage CV link.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://sites.google.com/view/ibraheemcatovic/research">
          Personal website · Research
        </a>
        : all ten titles, stated publication statuses, coauthorship, paper
        links, and the alternate CV.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://sites.google.com/view/ibraheemcatovic/teaching">
          Personal website · Teaching
        </a>
        : all seven courses and 23 syllabus links, preserved in this concept.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href={profile.cv}>Homepage CV · August 2025</a>: education,
        employment history, professional address, and LinkedIn link.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://doi.org/10.1017/esa.2025.10026">
          Cambridge University Press · Distribution-dependent number preferences
        </a>
        : author, abstract, journal, 2025 volume and page range. The short
        overview on this concept is an editorial paraphrase of its abstract.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://bulletins.nyu.edu/nyu/faculty-information/faculty-information.pdf">
          NYU faculty bulletin
        </a>
        : lists Visiting Clinical Assistant Professor, Economics, and University
        of Maryland Ph.D.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://economics.sas.rutgers.edu/people/faculty/people/86-faculty/1212-catovic-ibraheem">
          Rutgers faculty listing
        </a>
        : also lists Lecturer (Instructor). Its currency and overlap with NYU
        are unclear; it is not presented here as a current appointment.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://api.drum.lib.umd.edu/server/api/core/bitstreams/509cafbf-0538-40e8-8e60-2508cddc1ce7/content">
          University of Maryland dissertation repository
        </a>
        : corroborates the 2021 Ph.D. and dissertation,{' '}
        <em>Essays on Decision Making Over Risk</em>.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <h2>What remains uncertain</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        The current appointment end date has not been independently confirmed.
        The personal site lists NYU, while the August 2025 CV gives September
        2023–Present.
      </li>
      <li>
        The homepage and research page link different CV files. The homepage
        version is used as the primary CV; both remain accessible.
      </li>
      <li>
        The original link for “What Determines Lotto Demand? Mega Millions, Hope
        and Regret” opens a draft of “Distribution-Dependent Number
        Preferences.” It is preserved with an explicit mismatch note; the
        correct file remains unconfirmed.
      </li>
      <li>
        The 2014 banking article is listed on the original site without a link.
        This concept does not invent a DOI or download.
      </li>
      <li>
        “Under review” is a readable rendering of the original site's “peer
        review” label, not independent confirmation of editorial status.
      </li>
      <li>
        The postal code 10002 follows the CV verbatim and should be confirmed
        before use.
      </li>
      <li>
        Paper subject groupings and introductory copy are editorial choices. No
        inferred paper abstracts, new academic claims, or synthetic portrait are
        used.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Independent design concept</h2>
    <p>
      Created by Academic Web Studio. This website is not affiliated with or
      endorsed by Professor Ibraheem Catovic or NYU. Research documents remain
      on their original hosts. No contact form transmits data, and this local
      demo includes no analytics. Search engines are instructed not to index the
      concept; these instructions do not make a hosted website private.
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
